  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (173 tests, 0 failed), including the new store and API tests.\n\n**Store (`src/store.js`)**\n- Time comes only from the store's `clock`.\n- `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm`, `release` and the `removeItem` change follow your spec.\n- `confirm` returns `{sku, stock}`, which the API uses for its 200 response.\n\n**API (`src/api.js`)**\n- `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`.\n- `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` return the statuses you listed.\n- `POST /reservations` returns 400 for any error other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK`, which is 409.\n\n**Not in your spec**\n- Reservation ids look like `res-1`, `res-2`, and so on.\n- `ttlMs` is not validated, so a missing or non-numeric value makes the reservation's expiry `NaN`, and it never expires.\n- Expired reservations stay in memory until they are released. This doesn't affect availability, but the map grows over time.\n\n**Tests**\n- `test/store.test.js` covers availability, expiry at exactly creation time plus `ttlMs`, confirm and release, and `removeItem` against reserved stock.\n- `test/api.test.js` covers the 201, 409, 400, 200, 404, 410 and 204 responses.",
